data: {"type":"reasoning","text":"We need to create a simple Node.js application in current project folder. The folder appears to be empty. Need to create server.mjs, a directory for data maybe data/tasks.json? tests file maybe server.mjs tests? We'll use node's http module, ESM, no dependencies. Provide interface HTML/CSS/JS maybe index.html in root. Data storage in JSON local file tasks.json. Provide endpoints: GET /api/tasks to list tasks; POST /api/tasks to add; PATCH /api/tasks to complete; DELETE /api/tasks to delete (by id maybe). We'll implement tasks with id auto-increment. Use query string or body. We'll parse JSON body. We'll create a simple static file server for index.html etc.\n\nTesting: node --test will run test files *.test.js using built-in test runner? Node 26.0.0 supports built-in test. We'll create tests using assert, fetch? But no fetch in node unless experimental? Instead use http.request or fetch from node's global fetch available? Node 18+ includes experimental fetch but stable? We can use node's built-in http client: use http.request.\n\nWe need to start server for tests and then shut down. But instruction: no persistent servers or background processes. For tests, we can run server in same test code: import server.mjs, start it listening on port, run tests against it, then close. But need to export a function startServer? We'll write server.mjs that exports startServer and stopServer. For running node server.mjs manually, it will start the server.\n\nImplement:\n\n- server.mjs: use http, fs/promises, url. Data file path relative to __dirname? In ESM, __dirname not defined; use import.meta.url to resolve. Use fs.promises.\n\n- Provide function loadTasks, saveTasks.\n\n- API routes: GET /api/tasks list tasks; POST /api/tasks expecting JSON {title:\"...\"}; returns created task. PATCH /api/tasks expecting {id:..., completed:true} maybe. DELETE /api/tasks expecting {id:...}. Simple.\n\n- Also serve static files: if request target ends with .html .css .js serve accordingly from current dir; else 404.\n\nTesting: create test file tests/task.test.js. Node test runner automatically picks .test.js. We'll start server on random port like 3000; before all tests, start, after all, stop. Use jest-like beforeAll. Node test has \"beforeAll\" etc. We need to import 'node:test' and 'node:assert'. We'll use 'node:test' to define tests.\n\nIn tests, we need to send HTTP requests. Use http.request or fetch? Node 18+ has global fetch: stable? In Node 18, fetch is experimental; Node 20 stable. Node 26 likely stable fetch. We can use fetch: import('node:http'). Actually global fetch is available. Let's use fetch.\n\nImplement tests:\n\n1. Add task: POST /api/tasks with JSON {title:\"Test task\"}; expect status 201, response JSON has id, title, completed false.\n\n2. Complete task: PATCH /api/tasks with {id:createdId, completed:true}; expect 200, response updated.\n\n3. Delete task: DELETE /api/tasks with {id:createdId}; expect 200.\n\nCheck that after deletion, GET /api/tasks no longer has it.\n\nAlso test that GET returns empty array initially.\n\nBefore tests, server loads existing tasks.json maybe containing empty array. We'll ensure tasks.json starts as [] if missing.\n\nWe need to create tasks.json file initially empty.\n\nImplement server to use file tasks.json in same dir.\n\nTesting should pass.\n\nNeed to ensure server is exportable.\n\nLet's create files:\n\n- server.mjs\n- index.html (simple page)\n- styles.css\n- app.js (simple fetch to interface)\n- data/tasks.json (empty array)\n- tests/task.test.js\n\nBut instructions: \"Crea y termina una aplicación de tareas en esta carpeta vacía\" So we need to create files with appropriate content.\n\nWe will implement minimal index.html that loads app.js, shows list, form to add, buttons to complete/delete.\n\nBut tests just run server; index not needed for tests but requested to include.\n\nLet's create.\n\nProceed to make changes via archivo and reemplazar.\n\nFirst create server.mjs file."}

