isten(port, resolve)); That resolves when server listens. Good.\n\nThe test harness: 'node --test task.test.mjs' expects test files to use node:test API. Should import from 'node:test'.\n\nLet's modify task.test.mjs accordingly:\n\nAdd import { test, expect, beforeAll, afterAll } from 'node:test';\n\nAlso need to adjust baseUrl after server started; but we need to compute baseUrl inside tests where global.server defined after start. Could compute inside each test or afterAll. In current code, baseUrl defined as string referencing global.server. But global.server may be defined later? In test file, baseUrl defined outside tests, before beforeAll sets server. So at that point global.server is undefined; .address() may fail. So baseUrl should be computed inside tests or after server started. We'll compute inside test functions after server set, or compute after start server.\n\nSimplest: Move baseUrl definition inside tests after server set. But we can set afterAll? Actually we can set within each test. Let's modify each fetchJson call to use baseUrl variable resolved inside test.\n\nAlternative: compute baseUrl after awaiting startServer:\n\nbeforeAll(async()=>{ await resetTasks(); global.server=await startServer(0); });\n\nThen compute baseUrl within test functions using global.server.address().port.\n\nLet's modify test file.\n\nAlso adjust dataFile path: use import.meta.url with fileURLToPath.\n\nLet's patch.\n\n"}

