l afterAll? We need server start before tests. We can use beforeAll inside test? But better use 'test' with async setup: Use 'test' with 'test' sequential? We can start server inside first test? But better use 'test' with 'test' and beforeAll inside. But we need beforeAll. If not exported, we can do manual in test code: We'll create a global variable server in before tests by using test.beforeAll? but test.beforeAll may not exist. Actually test module exports 'beforeEach' etc? But if not exported, we skip. Let's inspect documentation: Node test exports 'afterAll' maybe. But error shows not exported. So maybe 'node:test' only exports 'test' and 'node:test' default? Actually docs say it exports 'test', 'expect', 'describe', 'assert'. Wait I'm going to check quickly: Node v20: import { test, describe } from 'node:test'; Yes.\n\nHowever the error indicates 'node:test' didn't export these. Maybe the environment uses an older Node? Node 18? It might not have test module at all? Node 18's test module is 'node:test'. But earlier Node 18 had 'node:test'? I'm not sure.\n\nAlternative: Use 'node:assert' and 'node:test' maybe missing exports but test itself is exported. If test exported, we can use it. But we can also use built-in 'node:test' test function? Let's check by running quick node test. But as ChatGPT can't. We'll assume 'test' is exported. We had error only for expect. Actually earlier error says: \"node:test does not provide an export named 'expect'\". Wait earlier first error when using 'beforeAll', it said 'beforeAll' not exported. Then replaced with onFinish still not exported. Finally we used import { test, expect } and error: 'expect' not exported. So maybe only 'test' exported. So we must write tests without expect. Use assert.\n\nAlso we used beforeAll, afterAll, but not exported. So we need to handle setup inside test directly. We'll use test('setup server', async t => { ...}) but we need multiple tests. We can use t.beforeAll maybe? No. We'll use global variable server and start before all tests in one test with 'test' and then call subsequent tests? But easier: use 'node:test' with 'test' and 'run' with each test uses setup code: We'll create server in a separate module before tests. Could use 'node:test' with 'describe' and 'beforeAll' maybe not exported. So we might just start server in each test separately? Could start server at start of each test, but that duplicates server start. We can start in a 'beforeAll' function by calling test() and storing server, then start server inside first test maybe? The 'node:test' supports using 't.beforeAll' within test? Wait 't' is context passed to test callback, and it may have .beforeAll? Let's check docs: The test function receives a \"Test\" object 't' with .skip, .only, etc? Actually not. Node:test's test callback receives a 't' test instance that has .skip, .todo, .log, etc. But I think .beforeAll is not part of that. Instead test module provides 'beforeAll' global like 'beforeAll' function. But if not exported, we can't use.\n\nSimplify: We'll manually start server in each test. Or we can use 'before' in tests by writing 'test' that starts server and returns server; then each other test will reuse that server? But not possible.\n\nBetter: Use 'node:test' with 'test' and 'run' but we can use 'node:test' to run sequential tests that share global variable. We can start server in global beforeAll by using 'test.beforeAll' maybe not exported. But we can use the global variable and start in the first test that runs, then subsequent tests rely on server.\n\nBut Node test will run tests in parallel? By default sequential? Node test runs tests sequentially by default? I think yes, test runner runs tests in parallel if not flagged. But we can set test run. We'll just start server in each test but close at end. But that may be heavy.\n\nAlternative: Use 'node:test' with 'test' and 'afterAll' maybe exported? But not.\n\nSimpler: use 'node:test' but with 'import test' only; then use